/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 48 0 R
/T (Low-code development is an approach to building software applications mainly through visual tools and configuration instead of writing large amounts of traditional program code. Applications are assembled using visual development environments, predefined components and templates. Typical building blocks include forms for capturing data, reports and dashboards for viewing it, and workflows that define how information moves through a business process.)
/E (Low-code development is an approach to building software applications mainly through visual tools and configuration instead of writing large amounts of traditional program code. Applications are assembled using visual development environments, predefined components and templates. Typical building blocks include forms for capturing data, reports and dashboards for viewing it, and workflows that define how information moves through a business process.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
